Open a terminal in your project folder

You’re already in ~/crypto-trader, so that’s perfect.

2️⃣ Create a new file

You can use a text editor like nano, vim, or VS Code. For example, using nano:

nano diagnostics.py


This opens a blank file called diagnostics.py.

3️⃣ Paste the code

Copy the Python code I gave you for diagnostics.py and paste it into the editor.

4️⃣ Save and exit

In nano:

Press Ctrl + O → Enter to save

Press Ctrl + X to exit

5️⃣ Make it executable (optional)

You can allow it to be run directly:

chmod +x diagnostics.py


Then you can run it with:

./diagnostics.py


Or simply:

python3 diagnostics.py

6️⃣ Optional: Add an alias for convenience

If you want a short command:

echo "alias bot-status='python3 ~/crypto-trader/diagnostics.py'" >> ~/.bashrc
source ~/.bashrc


Now you can just type:

bot-status


and it will run the script from anywhere.